  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe verifier shares model sections for geometric queries inside prismatic Z slabs of a ramped path.\nA flat cut plane keeps its own section. A sloped wall keeps the plane-by-plane reading.\n\nLaw (c) keeps the exact boundary samples from every cut plane.\nA shared geometric region does not prove that one sampled section covers every old collision sample.\nThe fallback sections each shared plane for the reach samples.\nIt keeps the original vertices, midpoints, and nudges.\nIt applies to small bands, near-tangent contacts, and large wall perimeters.\nThe fixed-spacing wall sample replacement is removed.\n\nLaw (b) asks the distance test before `edge_is_wall`.\nThese pure tests give the same result in either order.\nThe wall probe moves to `verify/section/wall.rs`.\nThe verifier reads the path. It does not change the moves or the posted program.\n\n## Review finding\n\nThe previous wall sample replacement lost collision coverage.\nThe review reproduced zero warnings where the plane-exact reading found 500 `ShankHit` warnings.\nThe shank met stock above the finished part. The solid law could not replace that stock check.\nOther cases lost findings with a small shank and a near-tangent contact.\n\nThe corrected law (c) keeps all original samples through the plane-exact fallback.\nNo fixed sample step is used as a proof of coverage.\nRead `docs/decisions/3831-verify-keepdown-speed.md` for the decision.\n\n## Performance limits\n\nThe previous 282 s to 1.2 s result used the unsafe sample replacement.\nIt does not describe this corrected implementation.\nThe fallback restores plane section work and the pooled samples for law (c).\nThe corrected implementation has not been timed on the earlier 38,432-facet plate.\n\n## Tests and pin proof\n\nThe exported verifier has three new pins:\n\n- `verify::slab_tests::a_shared_slab_keeps_near_tangent_stock_collisions`\n- `verify::slab_tests::a_shared_slab_keeps_small_band_stock_collisions`\n- `verify::slab_tests::a_shared_slab_keeps_stock_collisions_when_wall_spacing_would_widen`\n\nEach pin expects 500 stock collision findings. All three pass with the fix.\n`cargo test -p camcraft-sim --lib verify::`: 182 passed.\n\nMutation proof: restore the reviewed sample replacement and run the three pins.\nAll three fail: each reports 0 findings against the expected 500.\nRestore the plane-exact fallback and run the verifier tests again: 182 pass.\nThe mutation was removed before the final commit.\n\n## Validation\n\nFinal head: `d8700760c03683818adf67cd50fabb5a8c2b3cd9`. Base: current `upstream/main` `97a676e5c2307f7a2bc3c7677d1cbe334df8ef40`.\nHost: macOS arm64.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4`): 133 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. Sim lib: 265 passed, including the three new pins.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4`): 106 steps, 1 failed, 0 stalled. The failed step is `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`. The test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` gives planner counts `(4688, 4660, 1980)` against `(3158, 3130, 1141)`. These are the same counts recorded before this fix round for issue #3886. I did not run this test on bare main. The isolated known-failure steps fail as expected and count as passed in the gate.\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache cargo clippy -j 4 -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `app suites: example_catalog`: the quick gate ran `cargo test -j 4 -p camcraft-app --no-fail-fast --test example_catalog -- --test-threads=4`. Result: 43 passed, 4 ignored.\n- `app suites: example_catalog_adaptive` and `app suites: example_catalog_edge_work`: `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4 cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog_adaptive\" --only \"app suites: example_catalog_edge_work\"`. Result: 2 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `app suites: solid_law_goldens`: the quick gate ran `cargo test -j 4 -p camcraft-app --no-fail-fast --test solid_law_goldens -- --test-threads=4`. Result: 7 passed.\n\nThe first quick runs stopped at a build cache fault (`E0463`) after target seeding.\nThe retry with four jobs gave the same fault.\nI removed only the affected local package artifacts and ran the gate again.\nThe complete 133-step run then passed. No source change was needed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog suites and `solid_law_goldens` passed without updates.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"examples/catalog\"` is empty.\nNo recorded program changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The reporter's STEP model. It is not attached to the issue.\n- Timings on the earlier plate with 16 holes.\n- Windows and Linux.\n- A lower move count for keep-down ramps. That changes posted G-code and is outside this PR.\n- UI screenshots. No UI file changes.\n\nChangelog: The verifier shares prismatic model sections for geometric queries and skips distant wall probes. Collision reach checks keep the exact samples from every cut plane.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3831\n",
